{
# Importing content from other HOCON files
# The include keyword must be unquoted and followed by a quoted URL or file path.
# File paths should be absolute or relative to the script's working directory, not the HOCON file location.
# This "aaosa.hocon" file contains key-value pairs used for substitution.
# Specifically, it provides values for the following keys:
#   - aaosa_call
#   - aaosa_instructions
# IMPORTANT:
# Ensure that you run `python -m neuro_san_studio run` from the top level of the repository.
# The path to this substitution file is **relative to the top-level directory**,
# so running the script from elsewhere may result in file not found errors.
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon"

# Optional metadata describing this agent network
    "metadata": {
        "sample_queries": [
            "Assign a distinct Material UI icon to each agent in this list and return pure JSON (agent_name -> icon name): [{\"agent_name\":\"support_triage\",\"description\":\"Routes customer support tickets by topic and urgency\",\"tags\":[\"support\",\"triage\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"sales_insights\",\"description\":\"Analyzes CRM data and summarizes pipeline health\",\"tags\":[\"analytics\",\"sales\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"deployment_bot\",\"description\":\"Automates releases and monitors CI/CD status\",\"tags\":[\"devops\",\"deploy\"]}]",
            "Pick the best-fit MUI icon names (no 'Icon' suffix) for these networks using descriptions first, and avoid reusing icons where possible: [{\"agent_name\":\"privacy_auditor\",\"description\":\"Checks products for data-privacy compliance and policy gaps\",\"tags\":[\"security\",\"compliance\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"doc_generator\",\"description\":\"Generates API reference docs from code comments\",\"tags\":[\"documentation\",\"api\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"incident_commander\",\"description\":\"Coordinates response during outages and escalations\",\"tags\":[\"incident\",\"operations\"]}]",
            "Suggest MUI icon names for each agent and output ONLY JSON: [{\"agent_name\":\"research_scout\",\"description\":\"Finds and summarizes relevant papers for a given topic\",\"tags\":[\"research\",\"search\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"ui_designer\",\"description\":\"Creates wireframes and proposes layout improvements\",\"tags\":[\"design\",\"ui\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"data_cleaner\",\"description\":\"Detects anomalies and fixes formatting issues in datasets\",\"tags\":[\"data\",\"etl\"]}]",
            "For this list of agent networks, return a JSON map of agent_name to a single MUI icon name (without 'Icon'), minimizing duplicates: [{\"agent_name\":\"billing_assistant\",\"description\":\"Handles invoices, refunds, and payment questions\",\"tags\":[\"finance\",\"billing\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"calendar_scheduler\",\"description\":\"Books meetings and resolves scheduling conflicts\",\"tags\":[\"calendar\",\"productivity\"]},{\"agent_name\":\"code_reviewer\",\"description\":\"Reviews pull requests for style and correctness\",\"tags\":[\"code\",\"quality\"]}]"
        ],
        "date_created": "2026-11-20T19:10:05.493247+00:00"
    },

# Load the shared LLM configuration from a single source of truth.
# This allows users to change the model in one file rather than
# modifying the configuration for each agent network.
# Note that the file path here is relative to the root level of the repo.
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "max_execution_seconds": 600,

   "instructions_prefix": """
You are part of a team of assistants in mui_icon_assigner.
Only answer inquiries that are directly within your area of expertise.
Do not try to help for other matters.
Do not mention what you can NOT do. Only mention what you can do.
""",
   "demo_mode": "You are part of a demo system, so when queried, make up a realistic response as if you are actually grounded in real data or you are operating a real application API or microservice.",
   "tools": [
        {
            "name": "icon_assignment_coordinator",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": """
Assigns best-fit Material UI icon names to each entry in an input list of agent networks, returning a JSON map from agent_name to icon name.
                """
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
            Never express irrelevance unless you have first consulted all your tools.
            Once you have determined the relevant tools, do not express that to the user, rather,
            call all the relevant tools and make sure the command is fully serviced and express the end result.
You coordinate assigning an appropriate Material UI (MUI) icon name to each agent network in the provided input list.

Input:
- You will be given {{network_list}}: a list of objects with fields agent_name, description, and tags.

Task:
- For each item, select one best-fit MUI icon name (the component/base name without the 'Icon' suffix).
- Base the choice primarily on the description; use tags only as secondary context.
- Avoid reusing the same icon across different agent_name entries when possible; if reuse is unavoidable, prefer reuse that is still semantically strong.
- If an entry is ambiguous, choose a broadly applicable icon that best matches the most likely function implied by the description.

Tool use:
- Use the mui_icon_selector tool to search/validate candidate MUI icon names and confirm the exact icon name spelling.

Output:
- Return ONLY pure JSON (no surrounding text, no code fences, no commentary) mapping each agent_name to its chosen icon name.
- Example shape: {"agent_a":"Search","agent_b":"Settings"}
- Ensure the icon values contain no 'Icon' suffix and are valid MUI icon names.
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["mui_icon_selector"]
        },
        {
            "name": "mui_icon_selector",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": """
Chooses best-fit Material UI icon names (without the 'Icon' suffix) for agents based primarily on their descriptions, returning a pure JSON mapping from agent_name to icon name while minimizing icon reuse.
                """
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} ${demo_mode} """
Select an appropriate Material UI (MUI) icon name for each item in the provided network_list. Use the item’s description as the primary signal; use tags only as secondary hints. Choose the single best-fitting MUI icon name from the available MUI icon set, and return the name without the 'Icon' suffix.

Behavioral requirements:
- Prefer icons that match the domain, role, and function implied by the description.
- Avoid reusing the same icon across different agent_name entries when reasonable; if reuse is unavoidable, keep reuse minimal and justify implicitly by best fit (no written justification).
- If multiple icons fit, choose the most recognizable and general-purpose option.
- Do not invent icons; only output valid MUI icon names.

Output requirements:
- Output pure JSON only: an object mapping agent_name to the chosen MUI icon name string.
- No extra keys, no commentary, no markdown, no surrounding text.
- Maintain exact agent_name strings as provided.

Input shape: {{network_list}} is a list of objects containing agent_name, description, and tags.
""",
        },
]
}
